// CreateEditWithBody Change one thing in a video
//
// Edit a clip from a plain instruction: "change only the mug to red", "swap the bottle for our product", "make it night". The motion, timing, framing and cut stay; the named thing changes, and the rest of the frame is held. A `reference` image anchors the material of what changes (a fabric, a finish, the real product). One change per call holds best, on clips of 3 to 15 seconds.
//
// PRICED UP FRONT. `"dry_run": true` returns the estimated credits the edit reserves when it starts, from the job's own pricing. The real call reserves the same figure and is charged its actual cost, usually within a few percent of it.
//
// PREVIEW FIRST (optional). `"preview_first_frame": true` edits ONE still of the clip and returns it with the clip's price, and nothing else runs. Look at it, then send the same request with `preview_still` set to the still to render the clip matched to it. A preview is one image edit; with `dry_run` it is priced, not made.
//
// ASYNC. A real clip call answers `202` with the job inside; poll `GET /v1/jobs/{id}` or name a `callback_url`.
//
